  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Core Funding - Principles for Peace Foundation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Re-think and re-frame peace processes to address the key shortcomings in approaches to peace.
- Roll-out and implementation of new set of standards, norms, and guidance to better enable local, national, and international actors to craft more inclusive peace processes to contribute to sustainable peace.
- Through advocacy campaigns, increase awareness and uptake of Principles for Peace and the policy shifts to reinvigorate the global peace agenda.
- Collate and publicise good practice in the peace space and to develop practical guidance for national and international actors in their quest to convert policy proposals into changes in practice. P4P will establish its credibility to support decision-makers in key moments of design and development of peace engagement
- Inform effective policy making in peace processes through the development and implementation of measures to track the quality and effectiveness of peace processes; to monitor the uptake and implementation and effectiveness of the policy shifts proposed by P4P.</narrative>
  </description>
